# SPACBR — AUR packages
#
# Per §41-43 of CLAUDE.md: only add an entry when a specific, justified
# need can't be met officially, and note that justification next to
# it. The installer needs exactly one AUR helper (paru) to build these
# — don't add a second.
#
# arc-gtk-theme — the Arc-Dark GTK theme every gtk-2.0/3.0/4.0 config
# and xinitrc's GTK_THEME already assume. Not in the official repos
# (confirmed via archlinux.org/packages). Package name and existence
# now confirmed live via the AUR RPC API (curl from a real machine —
# the AUR web UI's anti-bot check blocks this from elsewhere), but:
# last actually updated 2025-03-31, flagged out-of-date by another
# user on 2025-11-30, still unaddressed by the maintainer as of this
# writing — a real maintenance-health concern per §42's "avoid
# abandoned packages", not just a theoretical one. Might still build
# and work fine (an out-of-date flag doesn't always mean broken), but
# hasn't been verified either way. Your call whether that's an
# acceptable risk for something this central to the visual identity,
# or worth finding/building an alternative for.
arc-gtk-theme

